 -- Phil <phil@brushpad.local>  Sat, 03 Oct 2026 17:31:00 -0500

lunduke-paint (0.8-2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Commit a floating selection before Save, Save As, print, and crash
    recovery, so the file matches the screen.
  * Flip, rotate, scale, crop, and canvas size keep a smaller layer inside
    its buffer and keep a meaningful layer offset.
  * OpenRaster load and save keep nested layer groups.
  * Merge Down respects the lower layer's opacity, blend, and offset.
  * Pencil, brush, fill, wand, and shapes honor layer offset. Thickness and
    eraser size spins affect the stroke.
  * Invert Selection keeps a full-canvas masked selection. Autocrop ignores
    rows it already trimmed. Undo back to the last successful save clears
    the unsaved marker.

 -- Phil <phil@brushpad.local>  Sat, 03 Oct 2026 17:05:00 -0500

